      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1904-12-17_WidnesExaminer_art0001" n="art0001">
        <p>COUNTY OF CHESTER TO WIT. NOTICE IS HEREBY GIVEN, that the next GENERAL QUARTER SESSIONS of the Peace for the COUNTY OF CHESTER will be holden at the CASTLE OF CHESTER, in and for the said County, on MONDAY, the 2nd day of January, 1905, at half-past Eleven o'clock in the forenoon, when the Grand Jury wil, be empannelled. The bearing of all appoals arising within the Hundrees of Broxtoti, Eddisbury, Nantwich. and Wirral, fermiog the Cherter District, and the trials of All prisoners com- mitted from such Hundreds, will take piece at sulti Se3sions. The Grand and Petty Jury for the Coester District must be in attendance at toe Castle of Cal ster, at the opening of the Court on MONDAY, the 2ad day of January, 1905, at half-past elevvn o'clock in the Forenoon. THE Court will be Adjourned to the Court House Knutsford. on WEDNDSDAY, the 4th day of January, 1905, at Eleven o'clock in toe F ireno an. The hearing of all appeals arising within the Hundreds of Bucklow, Diaccle3fild. and Northwieh, forming the Kauteford District, and the trials of all prisoner committed from tile last mentioned Hundreds will take place at such Adjourn.,cl Session 4. The Grand and Petty Jury for the Knutsford District must he in attend4nce at the Court House, Knutsford, at tbe opening of the Court on WEDNESDAY, the 4'h day of January, 1905, at Eleven o'clock in the Forenoon.</p>
        <p>REGINALD POTTS. Clerk of the Peace for the Cluntv of Chester, Chester, 12th December, 1904.</p>
      </div>
