      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1904-12-17_WidnesExaminer_art0017" n="art0017">
        <head>Housebreakers Arrested by Warrington</head>
        <p>Housebreakers Arrested by Warrington</p>
        <p>Police.</p>
        <p>At Manchester City Sessions,- on the sth instant, John Green and Isabella Bancroft,arrested at a house in Cartwright-street, Warrington, by Detective Superintendent Monaghan, on 19th November last, were convicted and sentenced to 9 months and 6 _months' hard labour respectively. As reported at the time of their arrest, this Kaan and woman were observed in town by Superintendent Monaghan, who enquired into their antecedents and ascertained they had come from Manchester. Manchester police were accordingly communicated with,and as a result Green and Bancroft were apprehended one morning during the small hours on a charge of housebreaking at Manchester.</p>
        <p>Carelessness in drying and exposure in cold weather will ruin the nicest hands. The skin gets rough and bard, and even cracks and bleeds, and the cold enters every time the wound opens anew. Zam- Bnk is a pleasant and powerful skin healer. If Zam-Buk be rubbed in, and an old glove worn at night, the skin may be kept soft and white all winter. Zam- Buk has the great advantage of being absolutely pure and easily absorbed, and therefore highly healing. Rub it in.</p>
