        <p>My last sketch is illustrative of a pretty and most comfortable cloak for evening wear, al- though it is of a mode which coul.i be worn in the afternoons if desired as a travelling or driving wrap. The material tiied is a iin2 loth, though velvet of a corduroy make would also look very stunt. It is made with he wide kimono sleeves bordered , with soft Jrown fur, the same fur formin; a flat necklet :ound the throat and falling, in stole. ends down the front of the gown. It is also en- aanced by wide bands of lace arranged in the :orm of an insertion, but applied on to the ;loth by dainty stitching in silk threads. The ,ame trimming finishes the sleeves. It could made either of lace as described or of silk embroidery bands, of which can be bought :eady made, or worked at home during leisure 1101111311 .</p>
