        <p>Widnes St. Paul's *Daresbary 4lO 2 5 3 12 20 5 Warrington St. Mary's Res l2 2 9 1 10 42 5 *Warrington St. Paul's ll 1 6 4 19 29 4 * Two points deducted for playing ineligible men. Results for Saturday, 10th December. Christ Church 1, Albions Res. 0. Daresbury 3, St. Mary's Res. 2. Warrington St. Paul's 2, Widnes St. Paul's 2. Stockton Heath Res. 9, Crosflelds 0. Matches for Saturday, December 17th. Warrington Albions v. Latchford Britannia, referee, J. Mather. Crosfields v. Lymm, referee, T. P. Fors. Christ Church v. Warrington St. Paul's, referee, J. Pendry. Warring ton Central v. Albion Res. referee C. T. Cox. Vulcan v. Daresduty, referee. Winstanley. Widnes St. Paul's v. St. Barnabas, referee J.Parry. St. Mitry' s Res. v. Crosfield's Res., S. G. Platt.</p>
        <p>Literary and Philosophical Society. The monthly meeting of the above society was held in the Masonic Hall, Bold-street, on Monday evening, when there was a good attendance of ladies and gentlemen. Mr. F. G. Ruddock, F.1.C., (president of the society), took the chair.—Mr. Congreve, Moore, read a highly interesting paper on " The Romanesque churches of Central and Southern France." The lecture was throughout illustrated with a splendid series of lantern views, thrown on to the screen by Mr. H. Houghton.—The Rev. H. A. Lester proposed a vote of thanks to Mr. Congreve.—Mr. Thomas May seconded, and the v ote was heartily accorded.</p>
