        <p>Hockey. [By R.G.P.] Once more the Stockton Heath first eleven had no match on Saturday,which makes the third blank week in succession. The match was cancelled owing to the New Brighton Wanderers' gronnd being covered with snow.</p>
        <p>The second team received a visit from New Brighton, Wanderers second team, and scored a handsome victory by no less than 7-0. Seldom have the second shown better form than last week, and on the day's play would have beaten most second teams. The goals were scored by W. Longdin 4, W. Howard 2, R. Fairclough 1</p>
        <p>This afternoon the club will oppose Sale land 11, and good games should result,thetfollowing teams having been chosen to represent Stockton Heath :--First (at Grappenhall-road), R. G. Pierpoint, goal; E. E. Woods and E. Pierpoint, backs; J. Richardson, Eric Fairclough, and L. Fairclough (captain), halves; C. H. Bond, S. Baxter, R. Pierpoint, W. Richardson and R. Fairclough, forwards. Bully off 2-30. Referee, Mr. Bellamy.</p>
